  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "An integer has **monotone increasing digits** exactly when each pair of adjacent digits `x` and `y` satisfy `x <= y`.\n\nWith an integer `n`, output *the largest number that is less than or equal to* `n` *with **monotone increasing digits***.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: n = 10\nOutput: 9\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: n = 1234\nOutput: 1234\n```\n\n**Example 3:**\n\n```\nInput: n = 332\nOutput: 299\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `0 <= n <= 109`",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
